cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ostadix-lang in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Ostadix-lang: Recursive Evaluator Composition for Whole-Program Polyglot Execution"
abstract: >-
  Ostadix-lang (O-lang) is a language system built on recursive evaluator
  composition: the evaluator for an expression is named by its delimiter
  syntax (LANG^( ... )_LANG), making the choice of interpreter a structural,
  compositional property of the expression rather than a global mode.
  Heterogeneous language blocks nest to arbitrary depth across a
  registry-extensible family of independently implemented real runtimes and
  exchange values through a single language-neutral value type (OValue).
  Programs lower into a unified intermediate representation (OIR) from which
  the runtime derives, validates, solves, and schedules a whole-program
  hypergraph (HGraph); arbitrary evaluator operations currently dispatch
  through the serial OIR executor. The repository contains the authoritative
  Rust runtime, an actively supported C17 interpreter and AOT compiler, a
  readable Python semantic reference implementation, and the O-core
  freestanding native compiler path.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ostadi
    given-names: Lee Daghlar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-6380-9558"
